  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A large ice-shell body with a sealed ocean and no detectable geological activity beneath it, warmed only by radiogenic decay in a mantle that has very little left to decay. The ocean is anoxic, alkaline and occupied by mats so slow that the 2255 and 2295 samples are, within measurement error, the same population at the same stage. It was named for the navigational method and not for any depth.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
